       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release in the US. That is about twice the limit, and it raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Immediate-release, at the max:** 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day).\n- **Immediate-release, lower:** 500 mg to 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals. This is the usual starting or titration range.\n- **Another intended dose:** If 1700 mg was meant to be the total daily dose, I can enter that as 850 mg PO twice daily.\n\nTell me which you want, or give me the intended dose, and I'll enter it right away."
      }
